WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.354
(bouncing music)

00:00:03.354 --> 00:00:05.240
- Yeah, I'm working with laser technology.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.640
I'm working with photons.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.250
Individual waves of laser light.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.912
It's tough sometimes, when
you're doing something

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:15.820
that everyone sees as
eccentric in its era.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.309
That you sort of have to wait
’til the next generation

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:20.229
comes along who looks at it and goes like:

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:23.229
"This isn't crazy. This is amazing."

00:00:24.184 --> 00:00:26.025
(telephone ringing)

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.521
Good afternoon, Holographic Studios.

00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:30.681
(plucking music)

00:00:30.681 --> 00:00:32.619
- [Narrator] Today we're in New York City,

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:34.129
and we're interviewing this guy.

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:35.841
- Jason Arthur Sapan.

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:39.098
- [Narrator] But his
friends call him Dr. Laser.

00:00:39.098 --> 00:00:40.499
- [Dr. Laser] Nicknames.
You don't choose them.

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:42.590
You get stuck with them.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.680
- [Narrator] He's a Holographer.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.720
That means he makes holograms,

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.750
and he's been doing it
for a really long time.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.766
- [Dr. Laser] This is now 41 years.

00:00:51.766 --> 00:00:53.640
- [Narrator] But not the
kind like Tupac, right?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.080
- [Dr. Laser] Oh no. Not even similar.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.497
I mean, Tupac's illusion wasn't even 3-D.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.320
- [Narrator] Holograms?
They get kind of bad rap,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.310
but they're actually a
really advanced science.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.368
- [Dr. Laser] Holography is a field,

00:01:07.368 --> 00:01:09.669
a subdivision of Photonics,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.648
that deals with wave recording of the--

00:01:12.648 --> 00:01:14.080
- [Narrator] Oh my God, science.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.139
Long story short, a hologram is made

00:01:16.139 --> 00:01:17.950
by bouncing laser light off of

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.379
a three dimensional object
and onto special film.

00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:22.568
Mostly.

00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:23.408
- Alright.

00:01:23.408 --> 00:01:25.447
- [Narrator] Holograms,
they've been relevant,

00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:26.949
a handful of times.

00:01:26.949 --> 00:01:29.819
- [Dr. Laser] In the
‘80s holographic jewelry.

00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:32.608
In the ‘90s, suddenly you had Pogs

00:01:32.608 --> 00:01:34.819
and Pokemon cards.

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:36.928
Oh my God, my son was like, you know,

00:01:36.928 --> 00:01:40.095
very big on getting the hologram ones.

00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:43.790
- [Narrator] There's no
denying that these things,

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.200
they're just not mainstream.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.418
But Dr. Laser doesn't care.

00:01:48.418 --> 00:01:51.120
Because he loves what he does.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.427
- [Dr. Laser] Maybe it
doesn't make me famous.

00:01:53.427 --> 00:01:55.600
Maybe it doesn't make me rich.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.990
But it makes me very, very, very happy.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.428
- [Narrator] Hell yeah.

00:02:00.428 --> 00:02:02.427
You do you, Dr. Laser.

00:02:02.427 --> 00:02:05.177
(plucking music)

